    "text": "Diagram shows the variation of internal energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;with the pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mole</mi></math>&nbsp;gas in cyclic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>abcda</mi></math>. The temperature of gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, respectively. Calculate the heat absorbed by the gas during the process.<br />\r<br />\r<br />\r&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0030772_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 225px; height: 208px;\" />",
